<title>JAPAN: Japan car export prices to US must not be cut - MITI.</title>
<headline>Japan car export prices to US must not be cut - MITI.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade Minister Shinji Sato said on Tuesday that Japanese automakers must not lower the prices of their exports to the United States because of the weak yen against the dollar.  </p>
<p>Referring to a meeting with U.S. Secretary of State Madeleine Albright on Sunday, Sato told a news conference that if Japanese automakers cut export prices in view of the yen's weakness, a trade problem may occur.</p>
<p>&quot;So, I think Japanese carmakers should not cut their export prices,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>During the Sunday meeting, Albright warned Japan of possible trade friction unless it fully implemented a 1995 Japan-U.S. accord on the auto trade.</p>
</text>
